From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: close SM8150 Main10 and encoder DMA gaps

Mirror the remaining wire-visible SM8150/VPU5 behavior identified by the
complete Xiaomi Q OSS line and function review.

For decoder Main10, teach the HFI4 packetizer to emit variable-sized plane
constraint packets, send the downstream P010 256-byte stride, 32/16-line,
256-byte alignment constraints, and reserve the downstream 4 KiB UV plane
gap. Keep format enumeration capability-stable while TRY/S/G_FMT enforce
the known stream bit depth. Add low-volume ioctl and buffer diagnostics.

Backport the capability parser payload-size fixes so mixed raw-format plane
counts cannot desynchronize SYS_INIT parsing.

For encoder bring-up, size linear NV12 exactly like the SM8150 downstream
VENUS_BUFFER_SIZE macro and map raw input bidirectionally. Snapshot both
policies at open so they cannot change beneath live VB2 mappings. Keep the
existing safety gate and staged checkpoints. Parse the optional VPU5 EBD
tail without raising the minimum accepted packet size, retain recon/UBWC
statistics, and reproduce the vendor bucket weights exactly. Log CR/CF
bandwidth inputs without changing the interconnect vote. RECON remains
metadata-only and is deliberately not allocated as internal DMA.

Invalidate requirements on format/lifecycle transitions and reset all
per-stream diagnostics before STREAMON.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
index b7d4f17c5751..d5dd7d534c34 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
@@ -491,6 +491,14 @@ enum venus_inst_modes {
  * @drain_active:	Drain sequence is in progress
  * @enc_pm_active: encoder stream owns a runtime-PM reference
  * @enc_test_stage: snapshotted SM8150 encoder bring-up checkpoint
+ * @enc_vendor_nv12: use the downstream SM8150 linear NV12 allocation formula
+ * @enc_dma_bidirectional: map raw encoder buffers for firmware read/write
+ * @enc_ebd_count: number of encoder input-done messages seen in this instance
+ * @enc_recon_index: latest VPU5 reconstruction-buffer index
+ * @enc_ubwc_cr_q16: latest VPU5 UBWC compression ratio in Q16 format
+ * @enc_complexity_factor_q16: latest VPU5 complexity factor in Q16 format
+ * @enc_complexity_number: latest raw VPU5 complexity counter
+ * @enc_bw_diag_ebd_count: last encoder EBD included in the bandwidth log
  * @flags:	bitmask flags describing current instance mode
  * @dpb_ids:	DPB buffer ID's
  */
@@ -566,6 +574,14 @@ struct venus_inst {
 	bool drain_active;
 	bool enc_pm_active;
 	u8 enc_test_stage;
+	bool enc_vendor_nv12;
+	bool enc_dma_bidirectional;
+	u32 enc_ebd_count;
+	u32 enc_recon_index;
+	u32 enc_ubwc_cr_q16;
+	u32 enc_complexity_factor_q16;
+	u32 enc_complexity_number;
+	u32 enc_bw_diag_ebd_count;
 	enum venus_inst_modes flags;
 	struct ida dpb_ids;
 };
